#X obj 460 2224 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 2200 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 2224 wsh2 \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2200 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 2224 wmx1 \$1;
#X floatatom 260 2200 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 260 2224 wmx2 \$1;
#X text 82 2262 Not on the Poly-800 \, all edges stay band-limited. \; pw1 \, pw2 (64) pulse width 0-127 = 3-97 % \, 64 = square: every \; foot becomes the AND of itself and a copy shifted by part of \; its period (pulse staircases on the saw net). \; sync (0) 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every 16' period of \; DCO1 \, at the exact sub-sample time \, swp2 (0) DCO2 offset \; 0-48 semitones \, continuous - sweep it for the sync sound. \; fm (0) 0-127 = FM index 0-8 of DCO1's counter rate (through \; zero above 45 \, integer ratios stay harmonic) \, fmr (1) ratio \; of the sine to the 16' \, 0.125-16 \, fms (0) 0 sine \, 1 DCO2. \; wsh1 \, wsh2 (0) Walsh loop 0-127: the 15 XOR products of the \; feet by sequency (0: 16' / 17: 16'x4' / 59: 2' / 85: all / \; 119: 16'x8' / 127 = 0) \, neighbours fade at equal power\; \; wmx1 \, wmx2 (0) mix from the feet (0) to the Walsh loop (127)., f 64;
