#X text 82 3974 Each voice's DCO1 and DCO2 have their own 6-stage DEG as on \; the Poly-800 (attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, \; release 0-31 \, setting one makes env1 / env2 -1). Measured on \; a Poly-800 II: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, attack rises \; linearly (31: about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and release fall at a \; constant dB per second (31: about 18 s to -40 dB). env1 / \; env2 (Controls) morph through: 0 gate / 1 short pluck / 24 \; pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / \; 127 long pad., f 64;
#X obj 60 4146 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Portamento 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 4204 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 4180 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 4204 port \$1;
#X floatatom 160 4180 6 0 2 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 4204 pmod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 4180 6 0 2 0 - - -;
#X msg 260 4204 mono \$1;
#X text 82 4242 Not on the Poly-800. port (0) glide time 0-127 = off to 3 s. \; pmod (0) where a glide starts: 0 from the last note played \, \; 1 from the note this voice played before \, 2 from the last \; note only while another key is still held (legato glide). \; mono (0) 0 poly (4 voices) \, 1 mono: one voice \, the last key \; wins \, every key restarts the envelopes \, 2 mono legato: only \; the first key of a phrase restarts them \, further keys (and \; going back to a held one) only change the pitch., f 64;
